Z||000006||Return of Fiero||11-20-2001||11:26 AM||||Even if this is somewhat commonly known, I have had taxis in Nashua for a few years. one day as a TIP(!!!!!!!), i recived my new 84 2m4. the only thing the guy wanted was for me to take it, fix it, register it, and show him the final product. so far, im 1 out of 4, close to being 2 out of 4. when i got it, it needed a new harness, and thats done. now im trying to figure out how to adjust the neutral safty switch (anyone want to e-mail me on how? ReturnofFiero@aol.com) and buying a new O2. then i have a trans leak to fix by the radiator, and nothing else. (as far as i know) <BR>Keeping my fingers crossed,<BR>Myke<BR>ps, fires right up with the neutral switch bypasses, and its been sitting since 94<BR>total cost by item:<BR>tow: $45<BR>harness: $35<BR>o2 : $20<BR>total : $100 Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
